# Aggie Playground — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. `.env.local` is
# gitignored — never commit it, and never commit real keys.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# The two NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the browser bundle, so they are
# PUBLIC. That is intended: Supabase protects the data with Row Level Security,
# not with key secrecy.
#
# The other three are SERVER-ONLY. `src/lib/server/*` imports "server-only",
# which makes the build fail if any client component ever imports it — so these
# cannot leak into the browser by accident. Never rename them with a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.

# ── Required for the app to work at all ──────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase → Settings → API → Project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase → Settings → API → anon / publishable key. Public by design.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Required only for the club-events feature (Context.dev bonus track) ──────
# Without these the app still runs; the Campus Clubs section simply shows
# "No club events yet" and the refresh button reports that the server is not
# configured. It never substitutes fake data.

# Supabase → Settings → API → service_role key.
# Bypasses Row Level Security completely. SERVER-ONLY — never expose it.
# Used only by /api/clubs/refresh to write the club_events cache.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Context.dev → dashboard → API key. SERVER-ONLY. Used only to scrape
# https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/events. Get one at https://context.dev
CONTEXT_DEV_API_KEY=

# Shared secret that authorises the Vercel Cron refresh.
# Vercel sends it automatically as: Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>
# Set the SAME value here and in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables. If it is unset, only signed-in students can trigger a refresh.
CRON_SECRET=
